      {
        "id": 115600,
        "name": "Craig",
        "username": "Craig",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/craig/{size}/2150_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-22T12:36:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think a lot of people are misconstruing my original question. I'm not asking if there are superheroes flying around; I'm asking if it's the same world. I'm not even wondering about crossover. In the fictional wider world of the game (which we don't care about and will never see in the game), could lots of time pass and find us in Megalopolis?</p><p>I don't want superheroes in my spirits, either. However, we know very little about the actual Sentinel Comics world at large. We don't know its history outside of the superheroes in modern times. Maybe this is part of the same world, just separate.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:47:49.371Z",
